# Repair Manager — project rules

## Stack (locked)

Tauri 2 · React · TypeScript · Vite · Rust · SQLite (`rusqlite`) · Tailwind CSS v4 · Radix wrapped in `src/ui` · React Router 7 Framework Mode · TanStack Form · TanStack Table.

Do **not** introduce: Electron, Next.js, MUI, Ant Design, Chakra, local HTTP API, React Hook Form, Formik, Redux/MobX, or `RouterProvider`/`createBrowserRouter` for primary routing unless an ADR is approved.

## Phases

- Implement only the phase the user explicitly approved.
- After each phase: full 12-point report, then STOP.
- Do not start the next phase without explicit approval.
- Docs: `docs/roadmap.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/coding-standards.md`, `docs/decisions/`.

## Architecture

- Frontend: `src/` · Backend: `src-tauri/`
- UI never touches SQLite or the filesystem; only `invoke` via `shared/api`.
- One domain = `src/features/<domain>` + `src-tauri/src/domain/<domain>`.
- App data only under OS AppData paths.
- Offline-first; no CDN fonts/APIs for core features.
- OS target: Windows 10/11 x64 only. Customer installer must work offline (`offlineInstaller` for WebView2).

## Features

Propose useful extras; do not implement without permission (SMS, cloud sync, inventory, invoices, auto-update, etc.).

## Quality

- Prefer small focused diffs; no drive-by refactors.
- New dependencies require purpose + impact in the phase report.
- Prefer performance over visual effects on low-end PCs.
